Description: vmwgfx: lay out per-plane offsets/sizes from the real height
 0006-add-vmware-vmwgfx-backend.patch inflates `aligned_height` to
 `3 * DIV_ROUND_UP(height, 2)` for YV12/I420/YUYV/NV12 — that's the
 size the SVGA hardware surface needs (one 2D rectangle big enough to
 pack Y + V + U planes top-to-bottom), and it's the right value to
 pass to `req->base_size.height`.
 .
 But the same inflated value was also fed into drv_bo_from_format,
 which uses it as the *per-plane* height — so plane offsets/sizes get
 computed for a hypothetical 540-row YV12 frame instead of a real
 360-row one. The actual chroma data the codec writes (compact YV12
 starting at offset stride*height) ends up well before the
 minigbm-reported V/U plane offsets, and AHardwareBuffer_lockPlanes /
 lockYCbCr consumers see zero-filled padding instead of chroma —
 visible as a uniform green wash for every soft-codec video frame.
 .
 Pass the real `height` to drv_bo_from_format so the per-plane
 layout is compact YV12 (Y at 0, V at stride*height,
 U at stride*height + chroma_stride*height/2), matching the AOSP
 c2.android.{vpx,aom,gav1,mpeg4}_dec output. The SVGA surface
 `base_size.height` still uses `aligned_height`.
Author: FydeOS <yang@fydeos.io>

Index: minigbm/vmwgfx.c
===================================================================
--- minigbm.orig/vmwgfx.c
+++ minigbm/vmwgfx.c
@@ -184,7 +184,19 @@ static int vmwgfx_bo_create_with_modifie
 	  return ret;
   }
   stride = drv_stride_from_format(format, aligned_width, 0);
-  drv_bo_from_format(bo, stride, 1, aligned_height, format);
+  /*
+   * Use the original `height` (not `aligned_height`) so drv_bo_from_format
+   * lays out the per-plane offsets/sizes for a real-size frame —
+   * i.e. compact YV12/NV12: Y at 0 (size = stride*height), then V/U
+   * chroma planes at stride/2 × height/2 each. `aligned_height` is the
+   * SVGA hardware surface size (1.5*height to fit packed Y+V+U), but it
+   * must NOT be used as a per-plane height: doing so put the V/U
+   * plane offsets way past where the codec actually writes (= compact
+   * YV12 from Y onward), so lockYCbCr / AHardwareBuffer_lockPlanes
+   * pointed consumers at zero-filled padding and every soft codec's
+   * output came up green on this gralloc.
+   */
+  drv_bo_from_format(bo, stride, 1, height, format);
   bo->handle.u32 = rep->handle;
   store_map_handle(&bo->meta, rep->buffer_map_handle);
   return 0;
